        "nobel_worthiness": "Cavity optomechanics and quantum acoustics made mechanical motion accessible to quantum measurement and control, opening a valuable experimental window on macroscopic quantum systems.",
        "attribution": "Cleland, Aspelmeyer, and Kippenberg represent major experimental strands, but the contribution is distributed across several foundational groups.",
        "maturity": "Quantum-regime control and measurement have been repeatedly demonstrated, though applications remain developing.",
        "uncertainties": ["Whether the field has a single sufficiently delimited original discovery and a defensible three-person attribution remains uncertain."]
      }
    }
